Thank you @soyuka, I pushed a fix and some perf on top of your commits.

`(array) $source` was computed before the lazy source got initialized, so a lazy source mapped to a constructor target lost its null values.

For the perf, on a 20-property DTO with two nested objects: 2.9x vs 8.2 with a shared mapper instead of 2.0x, and 1.8x instead of 1.4x on the first `map()` of a pair with a warmed cache.

One for a follow up: only class-level `#[Map]` pairs get warmed, so a property-level-only mapping with an explicit target never hits the cache. Warming more is free at runtime, the file is included once per process.
